    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_22ef8fca0a95c00ae0ba8d2382847ba3e557e075fbcc1f7993d4d318010aef83",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Rational separation makes the fractional-part weights periodic in the orbit period, enabling a finite congruence-class split, gcd reduction to units, and Dirichlet-character analysis. For irrational separation the source says that route breaks down and instead averages the equidistributed phase weights, replaces totient and Mobius factors by mean values, and integrates the period variable, recovering only the theta-independent leading approximation tP(t)≈1/epsilon.",
