    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_932cbe66dd8ac302089b82a3bb62391610059e0fe6ed9993c33b3a4cb35a72d0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The residue representation separates coarse asymptotic content from fine nonsmooth content: integer poles give the leading geometric term and other analytic power or logarithmic terms, while nontrivial complex poles supply zeta-sensitive corrections and are essential to reconstruct the exact finite-sum step structure. The numerical captions probe complementary limits, using scaled survival variables to test the irrational leading law and pole truncation with a second-derivative diagnostic to test recovery of steps.",
