    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_be64a94dad75b33f553c7253df266e42c1b0eea16e4442e420f1018963495500",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The conserved collision angle reduces circle billiards to boundary rotations; neighborhoods of short periodic rotations then supply the long-lived survivor measure and its finite period sum. Mellin transformation converts the shrinking-hole expansion of that sum into residues, while rational hole separation converts fractional-part weights into residue classes whose character projector and Euler products produce Dirichlet L-function ratios in the Mellin integrand.",
